codex
The proof will cover the complete input domain with two claims: the `n = 1` boundary and a symbolic `N > 1` claim. The expected result is defined separately by inclusion–exclusion (start count + end count − overlap), so the proof checks more than a copied implementation formula while still remaining tractable for K’s arithmetic backend.
apply patch
